{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis","id":837638,"title":"Help with understanding certain interactions with the Owls of Dis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-26T10:00:42-08:00","id":837638,"title":"Help with understanding certain interactions with the Owls of Dis","content":"Okay, so I'm playing a mixed Chronicles of Darkness game but I'm bringing in one of my favorite hold overs from Masquerade the Sabat. Vampires who believe that the Kindred belong ruling the world not playing dress up as humanity but as a Covenant not as a group of clans. The Sabat's local leader has a plan to seize control of the god machine and use it for what he believes it's true purpose is to make gods. He will become a god, and his people will rule the world.<br /> <br /> That said...the players...have no idea who he is other than a name that leads to a false ID that leads to a cat's paw, that bounces around a few more people and ends up nowhere. Just yet. His big reveal won't be till later but for now that have met his Mekhet spy &quot;Alexander Bell&quot;, or was it &quot;Ted Fitzgerald&quot; or was it &quot;Steven Crane&quot;. Now when they face off against Mr. Bell tonight they this mixed group of 2 werewolves, a Vampire, and a beast (LOOOOOOONG story, it makes sense because they are playing themselves and were friends before their changes, and the death of a close friend drove all of them different directions).<br /> <br /> I want them to face bell but the two Forsaken will rip him apart like he's made of tissue paper and the beast is an Eshimaki dragon so if you guessed they can breath fire, your very right. So I thought what if he could summon up some help that wouldn't be so easy to kill. My first thought was a small band of 2 or three Stryx thought I wonder does the Werewolf rule about being able to inflict lethal damage effect Stryx? Does dragon fire (a flame thrower attack) cause lethal or bashing damage? or does it only do Lethal when it would do aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> So why am I asking this here? Well I figure if anyone knows about the Owls of Dis it's the Requiem forum. So? Help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:29:28-08:00","id":837653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis#post837638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder does the Werewolf rule about being able to inflict lethal damage effect Stryx?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They only take damage from special Aggravated damage attacks, which is then reduced to Bashing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does dragon fire (a flame thrower attack) cause lethal or bashing damage? or does it only do Lethal when it would do aggravated damage? </div> </div> </div>Neither. Strix don't take damage by fire unless they're completely surrounded by it, which the blasts of Dragonfire don't seem to do. As long as they can escape,they won't take damage. If you use a Satiety Expenditure, however, it ups to Aggravated damage which, then, may cause Bashing damage to the strix. Also it allows you to burn other things, which can set a fire around the strix and potentially trap them.<br /> <br /> This is referring to 'loose' Strix, who are not possessing anyone and exist as shadows and darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:49:11-08:00","id":837662,"title":"","content":"So, usual disclaimer: crossover always creates weird edge cases and at the end of the day the answer will always be the one that best suits your chronicle. Now that that's out of the way, here's my input on this situation.<br /> <br /> Strix are not spirits and don't have Rank. No matter how high a werewolf's Honorary Rank, it's not higher than the Strix's Rank, since the Strix doesn't have a Rank to be higher than. Shadow Potency works similarly to Rank, so you could argue that a werewolf's teeth count as a Bane to a Strix with lower Shadow Potency than the werewolf's Honorary Rank. However, Strix Banes don't work the same way as ephemeral entity Banes do. Strix Banes work like vampire Banes do, they're not substances that harm the Strix, they're behavioral restrictions mined from vampire folklore, and more akin to ephemeral entity Bans than anything else. So pretty much any way you slice it, I don't see werewolves' natural weapons doing agg to Strix.<br /> <br /> As for fire, it doesn't do damage to Strix at all. Instead, fire (and sunlight) is solid to Strix. It forms an impenetrable barrier to them, which is useful for herding them around the battlefield, but probably won't kill them. If the Strix is surrounded on all sides by fire with no means of escape, then it takes one point of lethal damage per minute until they die or they somehow manage to escape (like if the fire goes out). Trapping a Strix in this manner would be extremely difficult with a flamethrower-like fire breath attack for a couple reasons. For one thing, being hit by the jet of fire would simply push them back. For another, in shadow form they can fly and slip through any gap that isn't airtight, so unless you can somehow create a complete sphere of flames around it, and sustain it long enough to kill the Strix, it's probably going to escape. Your best bet is to get the Strix to embody itself in a corpse or a vampire, and torch the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:07:00-08:00","id":837670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837653#post837653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They only take damage from special Aggravated damage attacks, which is then reduced to Bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh that is nastier than I thought maybe a pair of Stryx might be too much for them when you add in the Vampire Summoner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837653#post837653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither. Strix don't take damage by fire unless they're completely surrounded by it, which the blasts of Dragonfire don't seem to do. As long as they can escape,they won't take damage. If you use a Satiety Expenditure, however, it ups to Aggravated damage which, then, may cause Bashing damage to the strix. Also it allows you to burn other things, which can set a fire around the strix and potentially trap them.<br /> <br /> This is referring to 'loose' Strix, who are not possessing anyone and exist as shadows and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837662#post837662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, usual disclaimer: crossover always creates weird edge cases and at the end of the day the answer will always be the one that best suits your chronicle. Now that that's out of the way, here's my input on this situation.<br /> <br /> Strix are not spirits and don't have Rank. No matter how high a werewolf's Honorary Rank, it's not higher than the Strix's Rank, since the Strix doesn't have a Rank to be higher than. Shadow Potency works similarly to Rank, so you could argue that a werewolf's teeth count as a Bane to a Strix with lower Shadow Potency than the werewolf's Honorary Rank. However, Strix Banes don't work the same way as ephemeral entity Banes do. Strix Banes work like vampire Banes do, they're not substances that harm the Strix, they're behavioral restrictions mined from vampire folklore, and more akin to ephemeral entity Bans than anything else. So pretty much any way you slice it, I don't see werewolves' natural weapons doing agg to Strix.<br /> <br /> As for fire, it doesn't do damage to Strix at all. Instead, fire (and sunlight) is solid to Strix. It forms an impenetrable barrier to them, which is useful for herding them around the battlefield, but probably won't kill them. If the Strix is surrounded on all sides by fire with no means of escape, then it takes one point of lethal damage per minute until they die or they somehow manage to escape (like if the fire goes out). Trapping a Strix in this manner would be extremely difficult with a flamethrower-like fire breath attack for a couple reasons. For one thing, being hit by the jet of fire would simply push them back. For another, in shadow form they can fly and slip through any gap that isn't airtight, so unless you can somehow create a complete sphere of flames around it, and sustain it long enough to kill the Strix, it's probably going to escape. Your best bet is to get the Strix to embody itself in a corpse or a vampire, and torch the body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking more at the Werewolf rule that says that natural weapon attacks always count as lethal even when something has a special rule that says that the damage should always count as bashing. I hadn't even thought of the Bane effect. I just thought they would be able to attack them and hurt them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:42:07-08:00","id":837692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837670#post837670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking more at the Werewolf rule that says that natural weapon attacks always count as lethal even when something has a special rule that says that the damage should always count as bashing. I hadn't even thought of the Bane effect. I just thought they would be able to attack them and hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, gotcha! Sorry for the misunderstanding. Yeah, as Nofather pointed out, Strix are immune to anything that doesn't do aggravated damage, and then they reduce that to bashing. They're crazy hard to kill. As for werewolf teeth, they do lethal in all forms (including Hishu, which is cool) and count as a supernatural source of damage. This gets around things like a vampire's damage reduction, or anything else that works against mundane weapons but not against supernatural attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:49:36-08:00","id":837782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837670#post837670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking more at the Werewolf rule that says that natural weapon attacks always count as lethal even when something has a special rule that says that the damage should always count as bashing. I hadn't even thought of the Bane effect. I just thought they would be able to attack them and hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is actually incorrect. First of all, its not &quot;natural weapon attacks&quot; that hurt vampires that way. Its specifically <i>bites.</i> Uratha claws deal bashing damage, even in Garou form, while even Hishu teeth deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Secondly, we're talking about a natural weakness of vampires, and not an advantage werewolves have over vampires. Vampires take lethal from fellow vampires as well as werewolves using their teeth to tear in their bodies, while claws need magical enhancements to do the same. I would argue that a Beast would have the same issue - being eaten by another predator is bad for vamps, being clawed is relatively okay. <br /> <br /> In either case, however, unless a strix is possessing the body of a vampire, they're immune to this particular quirk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:52:44-08:00","id":837783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837782#post837782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is actually incorrect. First of all, its not &amp;quot;natural weapon attacks&amp;quot; that hurt vampires that way. Its specifically <i>bites.</i> Uratha claws deal bashing damage, even in Garou form, while even Hishu teeth deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Secondly, we're talking about a natural weakness of vampires, and not an advantage werewolves have over vampires. Vampires take lethal from fellow vampires as well as werewolves using their teeth to tear in their bodies, while claws need magical enhancements to do the same. I would argue that a Beast would have the same issue - being eaten by another predator is bad for vamps, being clawed is relatively okay. <br /> <br /> In either case, however, unless a strix is possessing the body of a vampire, they're immune to this particular quirk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, it's the host body that takes the damage, not the Strix's corpus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:58:58-08:00","id":837788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837782#post837782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, we're talking about a natural weakness of vampires, and not an advantage werewolves have over vampires. Vampires take lethal from fellow vampires as well as werewolves using their teeth to tear in their bodies, while claws need magical enhancements to do the same. I would argue that a Beast would have the same issue - being eaten by another predator is bad for vamps, being clawed is relatively okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's an advantage werewolves have over vampires. <br /> <br /> 'Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources. Even in Hishu, a werewolf\u2019s bite causes lethal damage to vampires.'<br /> <br /> Adding 'bite attacks do lethal to vampires from any source' would be a strange homebrew. You're fine to do it but it's not something the books are implying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:07:29-08:00","id":837790,"title":"","content":"Its an advantage that vampires have over other vampires as well. Its not something innate to werewolf nature, but a weakness built into vampire bodies. Werewolves, as similar predators, can take advantage of that weakness as well, just like vampires can sense werewolf auras like Predator Auras. The two have a strange relationship because they're both predator species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:22:12-08:00","id":837793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837653#post837653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is referring to 'loose' Strix, who are not possessing anyone and exist as shadows and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been mentioned a couple times but is worth underlining. A strix using its Embodiments to manipulate a body can suffer physical damage to the body, but that doesn't directly injure the strix. It only breaks down the vehicle it's currently riding. When the text describes the strix's natural form outside a stolen body as a shadow owl, it's being literal. Their native form is darkness. Not shadowy ephemera, but actual shadows. You can't bite darkness. You can't wrestle darkness. You can ward it away with light, or manipulate it directly with certain very specific powers, but that's the main reason strix are so untouchable outside exploiting their banes.<br /> <br /> Since you're using them as reinforcements for the Sabbat, you might want to use <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">the Khaibit bloodline</a> as the basis for a Lasombra-inspired cross-clan lineage, to use their influence over shadows and the Abyss as an explanation for why strix might ally with or serve a Sabbat vampire. Or you might play up a further layer of paranoia by implying some uncertain number of Sabbat might in fact be strix controlling Kindred bodies, stirring the pot. Or something between: perhaps the strix come to the Sabbat's aid <i>unbidden,</i> and the Sabbat don't really know what to make of it, or whether to trust their capricious new &quot;allies.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:58:56-08:00","id":837805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837790#post837790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its an advantage that vampires have over other vampires as well. Its not something innate to werewolf nature, but a weakness built into vampire bodies. Werewolves, as similar predators, can take advantage of that weakness as well, just like vampires can sense werewolf auras like Predator Auras. The two have a strange relationship because they're both predator species.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a weird way to describe it, since werewolves wouldn't be able to exploit that if their teeth didn't carry a mystic resonance to begin with. They're only taking advantage of a weakness built into vampire bodies in that they're bypassing a logical advantage against most things, with their supernatural nature imposing itself over the equally suspect resilience of cursed undeath.<br /> <br /> Considering vampire fangs are the means by which they steal not only fluid but<i> life</i> from others to distill it into the essential elixir that animates their unnatural forms, and how Blood calls out to Blood, I'm again more inclined to consider kindred dealing lethal to each other with bites an advantage of their fangs as opposed to an inherent weakness of their condition. It brings to mind how werewolves can deal aggravated to wolves or humans by consuming their flesh and ripping out the essence soaking it in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-26-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T16:34:43-08:00","id":837809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837790#post837790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its an advantage that vampires have over other vampires as well. Its not something innate to werewolf nature, but a weakness built into vampire bodies. Werewolves, as similar predators, can take advantage of that weakness as well, just like vampires can sense werewolf auras like Predator Auras. The two have a strange relationship because they're both predator species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... It's not an advantage anyone has over vampires. Vampires have the advantage over everything else that they only take bashing damage from non-magical weapons. Both vampires and werewolves have bite attacks that deal lethal damage and are considered magical weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T16:56:27-08:00","id":837813,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile.<br /> <br /> While strix make great antagonists, I question their placement as extras to make a fight more dangerous. While they do have some direct combat abilities, they are pretty simple, causing others to lose a turn or changing their damage to Aggravated. Coupling this with the sheer difficulty of actually doing harm to them, often requiring research to take advantage of their bane, they're likely to survive the death of the 'boss,' and be really hard to get rid of afterward. You can change this by having them possess someone, but at that point you may as well be using a zombie, revenant, human or vampire to begin with.<br /> <br /> Strix seem better suited for a more insidious or long-term threat, rather than extra meat shields to make combat more dramatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T17:29:45-08:00","id":837823,"title":"","content":"That's just it. Its not a &quot;magical weapon.&quot; That's the part that I'm saying is flawed. Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them; its a different kind of weakness than fire and sunlight, but its still a weakness. Werewolves and vampires don't have &quot;magical weaponry&quot; that bypasses &quot;Damage Reduction&quot; like a D&amp;D game. That's a holdover from D&amp;D thinking.<br /> <br /> If it was just &quot;magical natural weapons,&quot; then protean / werewolf claws would all work. They don't. In both cases, we're dealing with supernatural predators that use biting to hurt another. There's something about a vampire that makes them weak against the bites of supernatural predators. Its symbolic, much like how the pain of fire has to do with the idea of cleansing, and light versus darkness symbology.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm making a point is that there's nothing special about werewolf fangs other than the fact that they're from werewolves. They're no more magical than the rest of the werewolf. There's no magical properties in the bite that aren't in the claws as well. But vampires are weak to supernatural predator fangs, so werewolf and vampire fangs both qualify. That's why claws don't work, but fangs of both vamps and wolves, even when they're not sharp and pointy, but dull like a regular human's.<br /> <br /> EDIT - and, by &quot;advantage&quot; I just meant it was an quirk that was shared - two supernatural predators that have the same effect, nothing more intended or implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-26-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:00:38-08:00","id":837832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it. Its not a &quot;magical weapon.&quot; That's the part that I'm saying is flawed. Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them; its a different kind of weakness than fire and sunlight, but its still a weakness. Werewolves and vampires don't have &quot;magical weaponry&quot; that bypasses &quot;Damage Reduction&quot; like a D&amp;D game. That's a holdover from D&amp;D thinking.<br /> <br /> If it was just &quot;magical natural weapons,&quot; then protean / werewolf claws would all work. They don't. In both cases, we're dealing with supernatural predators that use biting to hurt another. There's something about a vampire that makes them weak against the bites of supernatural predators. Its symbolic, much like how the pain of fire has to do with the idea of cleansing, and light versus darkness symbology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they've made a distinction between protean claws at 2 dots being mundane, and protean claws at 4 being unnatural (And thus bypassing). The same is true with weapons created through Cruac. These things tend to disagree with what your saying. I was pretty heavily involved in the discussion that likely lead to Werewolf claws not doing so also, as they originally were going to deal lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:22:49-08:00","id":837843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it. Its not a &quot;magical weapon.&quot; That's the part that I'm saying is flawed. Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them; its a different kind of weakness than fire and sunlight, but its still a weakness. Werewolves and vampires don't have &quot;magical weaponry&quot; that bypasses &quot;Damage Reduction&quot; like a D&amp;D game. That's a holdover from D&amp;D thinking.<br /> <br /> If it was just &quot;magical natural weapons,&quot; then protean / werewolf claws would all work. They don't. In both cases, we're dealing with supernatural predators that use biting to hurt another. There's something about a vampire that makes them weak against the bites of supernatural predators. Its symbolic, much like how the pain of fire has to do with the idea of cleansing, and light versus darkness symbology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you saw the quote above regarding why Werewolf bites do lethal. The's nothing in the vampire book about them having a weakness to predators eating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:29:01-08:00","id":837848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837813#post837813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile.<br /> <br /> While strix make great antagonists, I question their placement as extras to make a fight more dangerous. While they do have some direct combat abilities, they are pretty simple, causing others to lose a turn or changing their damage to Aggravated. Coupling this with the sheer difficulty of actually doing harm to them, often requiring research to take advantage of their bane, they're likely to survive the death of the 'boss,' and be really hard to get rid of afterward. You can change this by having them possess someone, but at that point you may as well be using a zombie, revenant, human or vampire to begin with.<br /> <br /> Strix seem better suited for a more insidious or long-term threat, rather than extra meat shields to make combat more dramatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has a point there. How about useing the horror system from CofD and create gargoyles? It can show that they have something that the other Covenants. You could give the gargoyles the unbreakable dread power. That would hold the beasty away. <br /> Also there a few thing you can do to keep your big baddy around he can have dominate 5 and possess people or vampires for interacting with the party.<br /> Or he himself could be a Strix and that comes with its own fun things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:40:06-08:00","id":837853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it. Its not a &amp;quot;magical weapon.&amp;quot; That's the part that I'm saying is flawed. Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them; its a different kind of weakness than fire and sunlight, but its still a weakness. Werewolves and vampires don't have &amp;quot;magical weaponry&amp;quot; that bypasses &amp;quot;Damage Reduction&amp;quot; like a D&amp;D game. That's a holdover from D&amp;D thinking.<br /> <br /> If it was just &amp;quot;magical natural weapons,&amp;quot; then protean / werewolf claws would all work. They don't. In both cases, we're dealing with supernatural predators that use biting to hurt another. There's something about a vampire that makes them weak against the bites of supernatural predators. Its symbolic, much like how the pain of fire has to do with the idea of cleansing, and light versus darkness symbology.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm making a point is that there's nothing special about werewolf fangs other than the fact that they're from werewolves. They're no more magical than the rest of the werewolf. There's no magical properties in the bite that aren't in the claws as well. But vampires are weak to supernatural predator fangs, so werewolf and vampire fangs both qualify. That's why claws don't work, but fangs of both vamps and wolves, even when they're not sharp and pointy, but dull like a regular human's.<br /> <br /> EDIT - and, by &amp;quot;advantage&amp;quot; I just meant it was an quirk that was shared - two supernatural predators that have the same effect, nothing more intended or implied.</div> </div> </div> </div> If what your saying is true then every changeling Beast should be able to get past a vampire unnatural defense. But thats not so and there are only a few changeling Kiths that allows there damage to effect vampires normally. <br /> Its does not matter if the &quot;weapon&quot; ability was formed or created magical but if the attack retains magical quality to it. Such as a werewolf's bite would do so because of father wolf. <br /> But a Demon sword from its demonic form would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:51:00-08:00","id":837855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Claiming that vampires specifically have a weakness to predators eating them is a stretch of reasoning.<br /> <br /> You're claiming that they take lethal from werewolf bites not because of the thing explaning werewolves do this to foes vulnerable to mystic sources of damage, but because they're weak to predators biting them. Aside from the obvious supernatural closeness, vampire fangs have pervasive significance and qualities that implicitly explain dealing lethal to vampires. Werewolf fangs are <b>explicitly</b> magical, and vampires are used as an example of where this trait applies.<br /> <br /> See also what Rani pointed out,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-26-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:24:13-08:00","id":837922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it. Its not a &quot;magical weapon.&quot; That's the part that I'm saying is flawed. Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them; its a different kind of weakness than fire and sunlight, but its still a weakness. Werewolves and vampires don't have &quot;magical weaponry&quot; that bypasses &quot;Damage Reduction&quot; like a D&amp;D game. That's a holdover from D&amp;D thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Cause what the book says is &quot;Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This includes most non-supernatural weapons.&quot; Sounds to me like supernatural weapons are not included in the things that do bashing damage to vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was just &quot;magical natural weapons,&quot; then protean / werewolf claws would all work. They don't. In both cases, we're dealing with supernatural predators that use biting to hurt another. There's something about a vampire that makes them weak against the bites of supernatural predators. Its symbolic, much like how the pain of fire has to do with the idea of cleansing, and light versus darkness symbology.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Protean 2 claws aren't supernatural weapons. They're mundane animal claws created by a supernatural power. Protean 4 claws are distinctly unnatural, and deal lethal damage to vampires. They're also definitely not the jaws of a predator. Second of all, no, vampires are not weak to the bites of vampires or werewolves. They take exactly the same kind of damage from them everyone else does. They have a resistance to other forms of damage, which vampire and werewolf bites bypass. And yes, symbolism is the in-narrative reason it works that way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I'm making a point is that there's nothing special about werewolf fangs other than the fact that they're from werewolves. They're no more magical than the rest of the werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I was very strongly opposed to the idea of werewolf teeth and claws dealing lethal damage to vampires when it was first previewed, but that ship sailed long ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no magical properties in the bite that aren't in the claws as well. But vampires are weak to supernatural predator fangs, so werewolf and vampire fangs both qualify. That's why claws don't work, but fangs of both vamps and wolves, even when they're not sharp and pointy, but dull like a regular human's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do, as you pointed out above. Their teeth have symbolic significance as the thing werewolves use to eat their prey, which their claws do not. Bites in Hishu form do lethal damage to everything, not just to vampires, for that same reason. Werewolf teeth also have the ability to do aggravated damage to humans, wolves, and werewolves if the werewolf swallows, which werewolf claws do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837823#post837823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TEDIT - and, by &quot;advantage&quot; I just meant it was an quirk that was shared - two supernatural predators that have the same effect, nothing more intended or implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the quirk they both share is that their bites do lethal damage to <i>everyone</i>. Vampites, werewolves, humans, beasts, demons, they all take lethal damage when bitten by a vampire or a werewolf, so it doesn't make a lot of sense to call it a weakness of the vampire body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-27-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:27:07-08:00","id":837923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires have a weakness to predators eating them </div> </div> </div>I sincerely don't think I've ever read that in a VTR book....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T22:22:27-08:00","id":837944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837848#post837848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He has a point there. How about useing the horror system from CofD and create gargoyles? It can show that they have something that the other Covenants. You could give the gargoyles the unbreakable dread power. That would hold the beasty away.<br /> Also there a few thing you can do to keep your big baddy around he can have dominate 5 and possess people or vampires for interacting with the party.<br /> Or he himself could be a Strix and that comes with its own fun things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly haven't opened my Chronicles of Darkness book just yet, it arrived in the mail just today and haven't had the chance yet. I didn't even know that was in there...and Hey! Brief Nightmares! I like this it's like Quick Characters for that other Onyx Path game I play. Nice! Yeah use the Horde level and that should work out for a few very frightening things to throw at them. thanks for the help. But yeah Bell is not quite middle management yet, so that tells you where the players are in the story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T23:08:56-08:00","id":837952,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing Bell is your Big Bad? Do you plan for him to &quot;stay&quot; with the troupe? If so you could still use what I mentioned above. <br /> Also glad you like my idea or at least got some ideas from my own. But I have a quick question about your Sabat, do they still believe that &quot;Vampire Gods&quot; are pulling the string of vampire kind? If so you could have them view the Strix in that light. Maybe Bell believes ascending to Godhood is the only way to be red of them. <br /> Fun fact: Strix destroys God Machine complexes and infrastructure by simply being near them for a few hours. They also have an understanding of the God Machine and its inner workings that confounds demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T07:58:36-08:00","id":838055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/837638-help-with-understanding-certain-interactions-with-the-owls-of-dis?p=837952#post837952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing Bell is your Big Bad? Do you plan for him to &amp;quot;stay&amp;quot; with the troupe? If so you could still use what I mentioned above. <br /> Also glad you like my idea or at least got some ideas from my own. But I have a quick question about your Sabat, do they still believe that &amp;quot;Vampire Gods&amp;quot; are pulling the string of vampire kind? If so you could have them view the Strix in that light. Maybe Bell believes ascending to Godhood is the only way to be red of them. <br /> Fun fact: Strix destroys God Machine complexes and infrastructure by simply being near them for a few hours. They also have an understanding of the God Machine and its inner workings that confounds demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Markove is the big bad. Bell is a subordinate of Markove's subordinate. Markove is trying to ascend to godhood. Bell will likely end up a sacrifice to the new God. Provided he survives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:33:57-08:00","id":840359,"title":"","content":"A few things about the Strix that might appeal to you.<br /> \u200bFirst: The Strix are drawn to coming death and destruction, meaning even before the volcano goes off the Birds of Dis are there waiting. It wouldn't be far fetched for them to work against those trying to spoil the coming good time. No, the book never explains how they know what's coming, just that they often appear as heralds of what's to come. Several cultures hold owls to be omens of death. They don't even have to be known allies of your villain, they just want him to succeed. At least far enough to unleash hell on Earth.<br /> Second: Until they reach the highest levels of potency and can solidify their shadow form, the Strix are mostly impotent without a host form. This means you can kill or destroy the host and defeat the owl.<br /> Third: Unless you find a way to trap the Strix (fire or sunlight, two things Vampires aren't likely to use) then once the host is destroyed the Strix will escape (evil cackle fading into the distance). This means your heroes can fight and even defeat the bad guy in battle only to have him rise up again, over and over again. Each time mocking them and making dire promises, then he takes someone they actually care about as host and really amps up the drama.<br /> Last but not least: The stated goal of the Strix is to teach the Vampires that they are supposed to be monsters, not pale imitations of humanity, and if that doesn't fit the Sabbat ideal what does?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}